// Reaction ward: the two riders D&D grants ("resist the triggering
// elemental damage type until your next turn" + "the absorbed power flares
// into your next melee strike") map onto two independently-precedented
// primitives stacked in one `SelfBuff` cast -- `ProtectingWard` for the
// former (same flat-DR substitution every ward in this file uses, since
// there is no per-triggering-damage-type resistance primitive), and
// `BrandingSmite` ("next weapon hit deals additional damage, no secondary
// effect", consumed after one hit) for the latter, an exact mechanical fit
// for "stored power flares into your next melee strike".
//
// `buff_cat: Some(RemoveOnAttack)` (same field `branding_smite.ron` sets)
// applies to every buff in `buffs` uniformly, not just `BrandingSmite`
// (see the shared `buff_cat_ids` loop in
// `common/src/states/self_buff.rs`) -- so the `ProtectingWard` ward ends
// the instant the stored strike lands too, not just on its own 6s timer.
// That reads as correct here: once the retaliatory hit consumes the
// absorbed power, the short defensive window it was drawn from is spent
// as well, not a mismatch to route around.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.3,
    cast_duration: 0.1,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(kind: ProtectingWard, data: BuffData(strength: 0.25, duration: Some(6.0))),
        BuffDesc(kind: BrandingSmite, data: BuffData(strength: 8.0, duration: Some(6.0))),
    ],
    buff_cat: Some(RemoveOnAttack),
    energy_cost: 25.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Abjuration), source: Some(Primordial)),
)
